course: dictionary
lesson: 13723
title: Not enough, in formal writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insufficiently is a formal word. It means not enough, or less than is needed. It is an adverb, so it tells you how well or how much something was done. «The chicken was insufficiently cooked, so Mum put it back in the oven.» The chicken was not cooked enough.
explain: Sufficient means enough, so insufficiently is its opposite: not enough. Look for what is missing. In «The students were insufficiently prepared for the test», something needed more practice, so the students did not get ready enough.
explain: You will often meet this word in science reports and safety notes. «The pipe was insufficiently heated, so the water stayed cold.» When a warning says food is insufficiently cooked, it means it may still have germs that make you ill. Ask yourself: what was not enough?
fact: Insufficiently means not enough, or less than is needed.
fact: It is an adverb, so it often comes before an adjective or verb, as in «insufficiently cooked».
fact: Sufficiently means enough, so it is the opposite of insufficiently.
fact: «Insufficiently cooked» food can still have germs that make you ill.
fact: A good check is to swap in "not enough": «The room was insufficiently lit» means «The room was not lit enough».
exercise: «The chicken was insufficiently cooked.» What does insufficiently mean here? | Cooked very well and tasty | Cooked too quickly, so it burned | Cooked with too much salt | *Not cooked enough
exercise: Which word means the opposite of insufficiently? | Barely | Carelessly | Quickly | *Sufficiently
exercise: «The team was insufficiently prepared for the match.» What does this tell you? | They prepared far too much | They won the match easily | They were too tired to run | *They did not get ready enough
test: «The water was insufficiently hot to wash the dishes.» What was missing? | Soap | A bigger sink | *Heat, because the water was not hot enough | Time to dry the plates
test: Why is food that is insufficiently cooked a danger? | It is too cold to eat | It is too big to chew | It tastes too salty | *It may still have germs that make you ill
exam: Mia writes, «The bridge was insufficiently strong for the lorry.» What does insufficiently strong mean? | Very strong and safe | *Not strong enough for the lorry | Painted bright red | Built too quickly
